From c77df0ef7736e0a377ce6b86e626862132c3580b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 06:40:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] target/dadao: finalize cfx timer retirement semantics
 (KL-133a follow-up)

Supersedes KL-133a initial pre-execute/TB-boundary accounting with the frozen successful-retirement contract.

Normal translated instructions retire after successful semantic operations; precise faults skip the hook, while successful noreturn trap, terminal syscall, cfx2rc dispatch and halt paths explicitly retire exactly once. The shutdown latch prevents halt re-execution.

Timer counter0 decrements only on subsequent successful retirements. Expiry sets private pending and common TIMER independent of masks; every async boundary re-latches common TIMER while private pending remains asserted, independent of enable and masks. One-shot and periodic behavior, timeout-zero arm deferral, and private mask eligibility remain unchanged.
